    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Receive PUSH Notifications",
      "Anchor": "receive-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "When LinkedIn evaluates applications for your job postings, it makes a POST to the EVAL_CALLBACK_URL which you have registered during customer configuration of RSC onboarding. As a partner, you must return a 200 OK status code to indicate that the application evaluation is successfully received by your servers. LinkedIn will attempt to re-send the application 6 times if a non-200 status code is returned.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Receive PUSH Notifications",
      "Anchor": "receive-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "As part of the payload, you will be receiving an application-evaluation-id. You can use this ID to fetch the detailed evaluation as mentioned in the receive exported application evaluation.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Receive PUSH Notifications",
      "Anchor": "receive-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Receive PUSH Notifications",
      "Anchor": "receive-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "The latest API version is 202604. Use this version in the LinkedIn-Version header for all API requests to access the most recent features and improvements.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Requirements",
      "Anchor": "requirements",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Requirements"
      ],
      "Text": "Respond to all LinkedIn validation requests.\nVerify validity of push event requests using the x-li-signature.\nRespond with a 200 HTTP status code indicating successful delivery of the notification to your webhook.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Validate the Request",
      "Anchor": "validate-the-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Validate the Request"
      ],
      "Text": "LinkedIn will use a secret key to generate an \u0022HMACSHA256\u0022 signature of the escaped Unicode version of the request payload prefixed by \u0022hmacsha256=\u0022. This signature is then included as an X-LI-Signature header in the HTTP POST request sent from LinkedIn servers. Use the secret key associated with your API Key in order to validate the signature included in the request.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Validate the Request",
      "Anchor": "validate-the-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Validate the Request"
      ],
      "Text": "The computed HMAC can be tested using a free HMAC generator. Using \u0022hmacsha256=\u0022 and appending the request payload, the computed HMAC should match the X-LI-Signature from the request when using the associated secret key.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Validate the Request",
      "Anchor": "validate-the-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Validate the Request"
      ],
      "Text": "Example: hmacsha256={\u0022id\u0022:\u002259a92119-3b72-4d2f-8e12-137a13180df6-1\u0022,\u0022type\u0022:\u0022EXPORT_APPLICATION_EVALUATION\u0022,\u0022expiresAt\u0022:1481402799192}",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Validate the Request",
      "Anchor": "validate-the-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Validate the Request"
      ],
      "Text": "POST https://{provided unique application evaluation callback URL}",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Webhook Endpoint Validation",
      "Anchor": "webhook-endpoint-validation",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Webhook Endpoint Validation"
      ],
      "Text": "Important",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Webhook Endpoint Validation",
      "Anchor": "webhook-endpoint-validation",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Webhook Endpoint Validation"
      ],
      "Text": "You do not need to register a webhook URL in the Developer Portal; the EVAL_CALLBACK_URL is must be configured during customer onboarding.\nLinkedIn does not share IP ranges for validating push events. Use domain allowlisting instead of IP allowlisting.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Webhook Endpoint Validation",
      "Anchor": "webhook-endpoint-validation",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Webhook Endpoint Validation"
      ],
      "Text": "To prevent webhook URLs from being compromised by malicious actors, all EVAL_CALLBACK_URL must support the Webhook Endpoint Validation flow, as specified here.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
